    bat_priv->algo_ops->gw.init_sel_class(bat_priv);
else
    atomic_set(&bat_priv->gw.sel_class, 1);
```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
bat_priv->algo_ops->gw.init_sel_class(bat_priv);
atomic_set(&bat_priv->gw.sel_class, 1);
```
Reason:
The initialization for the gateway selection class variable did not differentiate between the B.A.T.M.A.N. IV and B.A.T.M.A.N. V algorithms. As a result, when the initialization for B.A.T.M.A.N. V was executed, it would overwrite the value set for B.A.T.M.A.N. IV, leading to potential misconfiguration when both algorithms were enabled.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (bat_priv->algo_ops->gw.init_sel_class)
    bat_priv->algo_ops->gw.init_sel_class(bat_priv);
else
    atomic_set(&bat_priv->gw.sel_class, 1);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a conditional check to determine if the algorithm-specific initialization function (`init_sel_class`) is available. If it is, it calls this function to properly initialize the selection class based on the specific algorithm. If not, it defaults to a safe initialization. This ensures that the initialization is handled correctly for each algorithm without overwriting values unintentionally.

